{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Uz1FPx2Z5tRUfHX1ZaSjQn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-folder, local-first personal productivity and R&D control system built for J.C. Liechty. Grounded claims about what it is:\n\n- **A markdown-backed task/project manager.** Source of truth is plain markdown (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, etc.) â€” no database, no syncing. Tasks move through Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later states with optional notes.\n\n- **A self-contained local web app.** `anchor_gui.py` is a Python-stdlib HTTP server that renders the full interactive dashboard and writes directly back to the markdown files. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` on `http://localhost:8777`. `anchor.py` mirrors the same logic as a CLI and generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **An R&D \"mission control\" cockpit for trio-driven work.** Its largest subsystem turns each project into a per-project window for the researchâ†’planâ†’build trio (researchPrime Â· Crucible Â· Foreman). It ships real ConPTY interactive terminals (`pty_manager.py`, the one declared `pywinpty` exception to the stdlib-only rule), per-session git-worktree isolation, a durable session registry, cached/validated session + project summaries, stage handoffs, and runnable deliverable previews (always on a free port â‰  8777).\n\n- **Currently at \"v4 Project Cockpit.\"** The latest shipped surface (built by Foreman, 9 waves GREEN, merged to master `38fd70e`) gives each lane a status-light tile that expands an inline panel with a summary-over-terminal split, a one-time skill auto-load/greet (fixing the repeating-prompt bug), a claudeâ†”gemini engine toggle, per-lane doc roles, a cost/tokens/time rollup, a grass idea board, and type-aware deliverable launch. The current branch (`foreman/rnd-v4.1-cockpit`) is iterating on the Paradigm-2 tile board.\n\n- **Guarded by a daily self-test.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs at 5 AM, parses every file, boots a throwaway server, and walks the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (never the live service or real `claude`), writing dated reports to `health_reports/`.\n\n- **What it ships:** the GUI server + CLI engine, the R&D control modules (registry, sessions, summarizer, terminals, worktrees, deliverables, previews), vendored frontend assets (xterm.js, anchor-term, GWL brand mark), the healthcheck + scheduled-task installers, and desktop launchers â€” all stdlib-only except the single optional `pywinpty` terminal extra."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24747,"cache_read_input_tokens":20597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24747},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d233c25d-fdd2-4f41-8c6a-b9f25d979a1e","uuid":"012f9372-0970-437d-aa36-02e0d50ed003","request_id":"req_011Cc2HeBk2Efaq8ecozbyLZ"}
